    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b32712b8_e6d5796e",
        "filename": "core/riscv-rv32i/atomic.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1153134
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-28T06:05:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes.\nBecause we didn\u0027t add parentheses (load a data value from the address in rs1) for %1 in assembly code. So we will get wrong syntax (rd, rs2, rs1) without adding A.\nOr we can change the code to if we don\u0027t want to use A:\n\"amo\" #op \".w.aqrl %0, %2, (%1)\" \\\n: \"\u003dr\" (tmp), \"+r\" (addr)        \\\nThese code should work as well.",
      "parentUuid": "e9961d79_cbbc9fd1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "a4fccb2df4e54457e1dfa148eda299be0c0e0d82",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
